{"tool_name":"caretta","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"caretta","home":"http://www.bioinformatics.nl/caretta","summary":"Caretta is a web suite for multiple protein structure alignment and feature extraction.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T09:08:53Z","last_update_date":"2021-02-07T13:48:22Z","tool_type":["Suite","Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:caretta","credit":[{"email":"aaltjan.vandijk@wur.nl","name":"Aalt D.J. van Dijk","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Global structure alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0510"},{"term":"Local structure alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0509"},{"term":"Multiple structure alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0504"},{"term":"Pairwise structure alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0503"},{"term":"Protein modelling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0477"}]}],"name":"Caretta","owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1016/J.CSBJ.2020.03.011","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2020 The AuthorsThe vast number of protein structures currently available opens exciting opportunities for machine learning on proteins, aimed at predicting and understanding functional properties. In particular, in combination with homology modelling, it is now possible to not only use sequence features as input for machine learning, but also structure features. However, in order to do so, robust multiple structure alignments are imperative. Here we present Caretta, a multiple structure alignment suite meant for homologous but sequentially divergent protein families which consistently returns accurate alignments with a higher coverage than current state-of-the-art tools. Caretta is available as a GUI and command-line application and additionally outputs an aligned structure feature matrix for a given set of input structures, which can readily be used in downstream steps for supervised or unsupervised machine learning. We show Caretta's performance on two benchmark datasets, and present an example application of Caretta in predicting the conformational state of cyclin-dependent kinases.","authors":[{"name":"Akdel M."},{"name":"Durairaj J."},{"name":"de Ridder D."},{"name":"van Dijk A.D.J."}],"citationCount":5,"date":"2020-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Computational and Structural Biotechnology Journal","title":"Caretta \u2013 A multiple protein structure alignment and feature extraction suite"},"pmcid":"PMC7186369","pmid":"32368333"}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene and protein families","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0623"},{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Molecular modelling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2275"},{"term":"Protein structural motifs and surfaces","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0166"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"Caretta","home":"https://bio.tools/caretta","summary":"Caretta is a web suite for multiple protein structure alignment and feature extraction.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:caretta/suite/www.bioinformatics.nl","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":12,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2020"},{"count":1,"year":"2022"},{"count":1,"year":"2026"},{"count":2,"year":"2023"},{"count":2,"year":"2024"},{"count":2,"year":"2025"},{"count":3,"year":"2021"}],"doi":"10.1016/j.csbj.2020.03.011","pmcid":"PMC7186369","pmid":"32368333","ref_count":31,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1984"},{"count":1,"year":"1986"},{"count":1,"year":"1987"},{"count":1,"year":"1992"},{"count":1,"year":"1998"},{"count":1,"year":"2000"},{"count":1,"year":"2003"},{"count":1,"year":"2004"},{"count":1,"ye